  "question": {
    "text": "A certain radar operates at a wavelength of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. If the beat frequency between the transmitted signal and the signal reflected from aircraft <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kHz</mi></math>, then what will be the velocity (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) of the aircraft?"
  },
  "options": [],
